The most promising targeted variant is not quote-breaking; it is making the *single* quoted argument start with an Nmap option and attaching the option value, for example `-iL/flag`, so Nmap’s own option parser sees it even though the shell kept it as one token. I’m testing that first alongside newline/encoded equivalents.
